From: OpenCode <opencode@localhost>
Date: Sun, 16 Feb 2026 05:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] Catch NoSuchElementException in Watchdog HIDL lookup

On GSI builds, hwservicemanager can crash (e.g. shadow stack allocation
failure during boot memory pressure). When Watchdog tries to collect
thread dumps, IServiceManager.getService() throws
NoSuchElementException because hwservicemanager is unavailable. This
uncaught exception kills system_server, causing cascading restarts of
SystemUI and other system components.

Catch NoSuchElementException alongside RemoteException so a transient
hwservicemanager crash doesn't take down the entire system.

Change-Id: I0000000000000000000000000000000000000001
---
 .../core/java/com/android/server/Watchdog.java       | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/Watchdog.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/Watchdog.java
index 000000000..000000001 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/Watchdog.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/Watchdog.java
@@ -825,6 +825,8 @@ public class Watchdog implements Dumpable {
             }
         } catch (RemoteException e) {
             Log.w(TAG, e);
+        } catch (java.util.NoSuchElementException e) {
+            Log.w(TAG, "HIDL service manager not available", e);
         }
     }
 
